---
description: How to use the Virlo MCP tools correctly (intent-first research, async job polling, credit awareness)
alwaysApply: true
---

virlo-api-usage:

- Always check `get_credit_balance` before starting a paid research run. Virlo is pay-as-you-go against a prepaid balance, no subscription: hashtag lookups $0.05/call, trends and video digests $0.25/call, Content Research Agents $0.50/run, satellite analysis $0.50/call, tracking $0.25/cycle. Data Intelligence adds $1.00/run on agents and $0.25/lookup on satellite. All agent reads and tracking reads are free.
- Never invent search keywords from a topic directly. Write a concrete one-sentence intent first (goal + content type + exclusions, ~40-250 chars), then call `suggest_keywords` with that intent. If `quality.passes` is false, sharpen the intent and retry before searching. 3-7 specific multi-word phrases beat a long single-word list.
- Creation tools (`search_keywords`, `create_niche_monitor`, `lookup_creator`, `analyze_video`, etc.) auto-poll for ~25 seconds and then return a `job_id`. Full agent runs take ~15-20 minutes median. Hand back the id and check later — do not busy-wait in a tight loop. While in flight, `pending_jobs[]` gives a `retry_after_seconds` per item; respect it, and read `progress_pct`/`stage`/`eta_seconds` for live progress.
- Treat `finalized: true` as the done signal, not `status === "completed"` — a job can be "completed" with secondary AI analysis still pending. `partial_failure` is still usable data.
- `min_views` and `time_range` are system-managed at collection and are rejected by the agents API. Read tools (`get_keyword_search_results`, `get_niche_monitor_data`, `get_satellite_run`, `get_tracking_report`) are free to call repeatedly — filter by date/platform/min_views at read time rather than re-running a paid search.
- Prefer `order_by=weighted_score` (or `rising`/`growth` where offered) over raw view counts when ranking creators, sounds, or hashtags — raw views over-favor already-viral content. Hashtag and sound results carry lifecycle labels (`new`/`rising`/`steady`/`fading`); lead with those.
- `search_hashtags` returns the overall ranked list for a date range; `get_hashtag_performance` returns per-hashtag detail. Use the latter when the user asks about a specific topic.
- Recurring agents (`create_niche_monitor`) are free to create but bill $0.50 per scheduled run until deleted. One-shot agents (`search_keywords`) bill $0.50 once. Tracking bills $0.25 per cycle per item until untracked. Confirm cadence and standing cost with the user before creating anything recurring, and surface `list_tracked_items` / `delete_niche_monitor` / `untrack_creator` as the way to stop it.
- Naming: the unified `/v1/agents` endpoint supersedes the split Orbit (one-shot) and Comet (recurring) APIs. Those are deprecated and slated for removal but remain live, and legacy orbit_id/comet_id values are interchangeable with agent ids — prefer `/v1/agents` regardless. "Niche monitor" is no longer the product term — say one-shot agent / recurring agent. The MCP tool names still carry the legacy wording (`create_niche_monitor`, `get_niche_monitor_data`); call the tools by their real names but use current terminology with the user.
- Read `virlo://docs/agent-playbook` (an MCP resource) before starting non-trivial research — it has the canonical intent-routing and result-interpretation guidance. Also available: `virlo://docs/intent-cookbook`, `virlo://docs/credit-costs`, `virlo://docs/api-overview`.
